{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779979698,"nonce":"AlKQja+PZalkVb8CV8xHu7t0vNM=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDq90Xg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/191","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat: consolidate 4 SeaSurfaceLayer instances → 1 multi-source","message":"## Summary\n\nMigrate `bizzyboat_project11/config/nav2_overlay.yaml` from 4 per-camera\n`SeaSurfaceLayer` instances → 1 multi-source `SeaSurfaceLayer` block, taking\nadvantage of the multi-source / shared-buffer / persistence rewrite landing in\n[rolker/unh_marine_perception#20](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/pull/20).\n\nAlso adds `published_topic: sea_surface/lethal_grid` so the new\n`SeaSurfaceRelayLayer` (configured in the seafloor base via\n[rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#35](https://github.com/rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11/pull/35))\ncan stamp the same lethal cells into `global_costmap` for `SmacPlannerHybrid`.\n\n## Why\n\n- Today: 4 `SeaSurfaceLayer` instances (`forward`, `port`, `starboard`, `aft`),\n  each with its own buffer that `segmentsCallback` wipes per frame. No\n  cross-camera fusion; no obstacle memory across FOV handoffs; ~50% dynamic-mark\n  flicker on the 2026-05-26 deployment bag; small-buoy \"resume\" failures.\n- After #20: one layer accepts a list of cameras as sources; all sources feed\n  a single persistent, decaying log-odds buffer in `map_tide`. Cross-camera\n  overlap accumulates evidence into the SAME world cell (faster threshold\n  crossing); evidence survives the FOV handoff via decay-not-wipe.\n- Adding `published_topic` lets the new global-costmap relay layer stamp the\n  same lethal cells without a second projection pass.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- [rolker/unh_marine_perception#20](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/pull/20)\n  — introduces `observation_sources` + `published_topic` config schema. **Must\n  merge + workspace rebuild before this PR's config takes effect.**\n- [rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#35](https://github.com/rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11/pull/35)\n  — adds the global-costmap relay consumer side. Independent ordering: this\n  PR's `published_topic` is harmless without the consumer (just an extra\n  publication no one subscribes to).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Single yaml edit: replace the 4 `sea_surface_layer_*` entries in\n  `local_costmap.plugins` and their parameter blocks with one\n  `sea_surface_layer` block carrying `observation_sources: [forward, port,\n  starboard, aft]` and per-source `\u003cname\u003e.segmentation_topic` /\n  `\u003cname\u003e.camera_info_topic` blocks, plus `published_topic` for the relay.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] yaml parses.\n- [ ] Workspace builds with #20 + #35 + this PR (pending those merges).\n- [ ] `ros2 launch bizzyboat_bringup` confirms costmap_2d loads the single\n      multi-source layer without errors; 4 subscriptions established (one\n      `\u003csource\u003e.segmentation_topic` + `\u003csource\u003e.camera_info_topic` pair each).\n- [ ] Bag replay (2026-05-26, episode #21 — the small-buoy resume): obstacle\n      mark in one camera's FOV survives into the next camera's FOV; lethal\n      cells re-appear in global costmap via the relay.\n- [ ] Sim-verify before deployment per the original #19 acceptance criteria.\n\nCloses the BizzyBoat side of the rolker/unh_marine_perception#19 finalization.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}